---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Walking with Jesus — morning, midday, and evening Christian reflections.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      <strong>Walking with Jesus</strong> exists so people can meet Jesus in Scripture —
      not as a distant idea, but as the living Lord who speaks peace, truth, and love.
      These pages are a quiet place to come and see. If you are just beginning,
      try <a href={withBase('start-here/')}>Start here</a>
      (or <a href={withBase('de/')}>Willkommen</a> auf Deutsch).
      Common seeker questions live on the <a href={withBase('faq/')}>FAQ</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each day brings three short invitations meant to be read slowly: a
      <strong>morning</strong>, <strong>midday</strong>, and <strong>evening</strong> reflection.
      Every article includes a passage of Scripture, a pastoral thought, and a hopeful takeaway
      you can carry into ordinary life. The tone is warm and reverent, never loud — an invitation
      to draw near, not a lecture from afar.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are hurting, begin with
      <a href={withBase('hard-times/')}>Hard times</a> — short verses for anxiety, grief, fear,
      and other hard days — or a simple prayer on
      <a href={withBase('pray/')}>Pray</a>. Each week we also publish
      <a href={withBase('stories/')}>Stories</a> of encounter — from the Gospels, and careful sketches that point to Him.
      You can sit with
      <a href={withBase('readings/')}>longer readings</a> of Jesus’ teaching, browse by
      <a href={withBase('archive/')}>date</a> or <a href={withBase('tags/')}>tags</a>, or
      <a href={withBase('search/')}>search</a> the archive. Prefer a feed reader? Subscribe to the
      <a href={withBase('rss.xml')}>RSS feed</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      If someone you love is struggling, consider sharing the
      <a href={withBase('hard-times/')}>Hard times</a> page — or a single tag link for what
      they face. A small invitation can be enough. More gentle share links live on the
      <a href={withBase('share/')}>Share</a> page.
    </p>
    <p>
      Whether you are curious about Jesus, returning after a long time away, or already walking
      closely with Him, you are welcome here. Come and see.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
